==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|es|en}} {{term|calabaza|lang=es||[[pumpkin]], gourd}}, possibly from {{etyl|ar|en}} {{term|قرعة يابسة|lang=ar|tr=qárʕa yābisa||dry gourd}} or directly from {{etyl|fa|en}} {{term|خربزه|tr=xarboza, xarboze||melon|lang=fa}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|καρπός|tr=karpós|sc=polytonic|lang=grc}}, or from a {{etyl|und-ibe|en}} word *''calapaccia''; cognate with French {{term|calebasse|lang=fr||gourd}}.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|es}}

# A [[vine]] grown for its [[fruit]], which can be harvested young and used as a vegetable, or harvested mature, dried{{,}} and used as a container, like a [[gourd]]. In particular, {{taxlink|Lagenaria siceraria|species|noshow=1}}.
# {{context|originally|lang=en}} The fruit of such a vine.
# A utensil traditionally made of the dried [[shell]] of a calabash and used as a bottle, dipper, utensil or pipe, etc.

